{"reference":"Psalms 125","book":"Psalms","chapter":125,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Surrounding Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The surrounding Songs of Ascents are associated with worship and include communal memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, alongside thanksgiving for return, festival praise, and meditation on Torah. This broader setting is disputed, but it places Psalm 125 among psalms shaped for a worshiping community.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_125_c78b5cabec1f78ed0c8ef85d"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}